#!/usr/bin/env python3
"""tools/daily-bench-guest <step> [arg ...]: tools/daily-bench's part inside the test computer, put there as
/var/tmp/daily/daily-bench-guest and run as root through the guest agent (vm run -- /usr/bin/python3 -I
/var/tmp/daily/daily-bench-guest <step> ...). What the person would do runs as the person signed in, with their
desktop's environment, as tools/vm-smoke-guest does. Each step prints one JSON object as its last line: what it
measured, and for a daily task "ok" and, when it failed, "why". A task is judged by what came of it (a sound in the
speaker, a colour on the screen, an answer from the app), never by a window having appeared.

Times are taken on this computer's own clock: a key's press by the kernel's time stamp on its input event (the key
comes from QEMU's USB keyboard, sent by the cloud machine), a surface's showing by Hyprland's event for it.
"""
